{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130065-thought-experiments","id":1130065,"title":"Thought Experiments","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-16T18:12:52-07:00","id":1130065,"title":"Thought Experiments","content":"Wish I could come up with a snappier title, but this is basically a public dump of various mage related ideas I had, but haven't had the time to work on. I'll get around to them eventually (I hope), but in the meantime, why not share them for others to flesh out and use?<br /> <br /> I'll break these out into their own threads when I have anything other than the stub of an idea to work with.<br /> <br /> Oh, and if anyone else want to just post their ideas (on any of these, or their own half-formed concepts), feel free. <hr /><ul><li>[Placeholder: Spell-flayers]<ul><li>Concept: Discount Banishers - They kill Mages and turn that into power.</li> <li>I thought about creating a variant of the Dark Eras Skin-Thief merit. They'd have an instance representing each Mage they've &quot;skinned&quot;, but framed as that Mage's talents, rather than an Animal/Spirit/Ghost's.</li> <li>Option 1: How to represent and write down a Mage's Gnosis, Arcana, and Praxis? ...Artifacts basically <i>are</i> that already (though of a Supernal thingy, rather than &quot;Made from real Magus&quot;). Maybe these mage-killers make an Artifact out of a Mage and their Dedicated Tool? A mystery in and of itself.</li> <li>Option 2: They can force Mages killed to form Ghost Mages, that they then Skin the &quot;normal&quot; Skin-Thief way. Simplifies any created mechanics, but leaves them strangely vulnerable to Death Arcana.</li> <li>Option 3: Kill a Mage, get a Rote (or Rotes) of their Praxis (like a serial-killer Mega-man). Use Willpower for the casting pool?</li> <li>Option 4: I don't know yet?</li> </ul></li> <li>[Placeholder: Espers]<ul><li>Concept: Naturalized magical critters</li> <li>Basically, Build-a-monster, but the abilities are designed as locked-in Legacy Attainments (so no real casting pool, no Paradox, etc.).</li> <li>Had vague notions of an organization that is creating them. Via Soul-Shaping? But critters don't <i>have</i> souls to shape. And this is Archmaster-level magic. Left over Archmaster Artifact?</li> </ul></li> <li>[Placeholder: ???]<ul><li>Concept: Naturalized Artifacts</li> <li>That's just it - Artifacts with powers structured as Legacy Attainments (locked in, yes, but no Paradox).</li> <li>Maybe an Artifact exists in the Fallen World so long it gets acclimated? Tragedy or Boon?</li> </ul></li> <li>[Placeholder: Icon Enchanter]<ul><li>Concept: Make use of Space's Sympathy rules for magic.</li> <li>They can create Imbued Items with a Spell of a dot rating equal to the Sympathetic Connection to (whatever). Good friends lead to magic toys. Of course, if relationships decay, The Magic Goes Away. This would cap most of them at 3-dot spells (for the deepest connections, outside of one's self), making them about as limited as Proximi in power (if not in scope).</li> </ul></li> <li>[Placeholder: ???]<ul><li>Concept: Make use of Time's Sympathy rules for magic.</li> <li>Since time is based on how &quot;different&quot; something &quot;now&quot; compared to &quot;then&quot;, maybe a Boon/Curse like system could be used? The more one deviates from the target point, the more powerful the magic.</li> </ul></li> <li>[Placeholder: ???]<ul><li>Concept: A group that uses Sanctums, Demesnes, and Space magic.</li> <li>They use a combination of Space magic and favorable Sanctum/Hallow/Demesne conditions to grant remote benefits to members or clients.</li> </ul></li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-16-2017, 09:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T19:47:31-07:00","id":1130094,"title":"","content":"How do Espers meaningfully differ from Cryptids?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T19:54:00-07:00","id":1130099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130065-thought-experiments?p=1130094#post1130094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do Espers meaningfully differ from Cryptids?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Established rules/guidelines? Rather than just &quot;some strange creature a Mage might be interested in that doesn't fall into another category&quot;?<br /> <br /> Niche already filled?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T20:06:28-07:00","id":1130102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130065-thought-experiments?p=1130099#post1130099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Established rules/guidelines? Rather than just &amp;quot;some strange creature a Mage might be interested in that doesn't fall into another category&amp;quot;?<br /> <br /> Niche already filled?</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant the Cryptids from Demon: the Descent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T20:40:27-07:00","id":1130114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130065-thought-experiments?p=1130099#post1130099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Established rules/guidelines? Rather than just &quot;some strange creature a Mage might be interested in that doesn't fall into another category&quot;?<br /> <br /> Niche already filled?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Horrors from the Chronicles of Darkness also covers that niche.<br /> As described, Espers feel more like a 'Proximi animals' or &quot;Supernal-touched&quot;. They still have a place but less of &quot;I have never seen anything like this&quot; and more &quot;How did that happen?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T22:07:53-07:00","id":1130141,"title":"","content":"Wonder if a Supernal entity can reproduce with a Fallen World lifeform.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T22:24:12-07:00","id":1130146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130065-thought-experiments?p=1130141#post1130141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wonder if a Supernal entity can reproduce with a Fallen World lifeform.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would probably be super rare, but I don't see why not. Any Supernal entity with Life 4 could turn themselves into any animal they wanted, including human. A physical body would prevent Dissonance from destroying them and they could probably get around Mana bleed fairly easily if they were to latch on to a Mage.<br /> <br /> What would you call such children, and what powers (if any) would they have?<br /> <br /> I'd call the offspring of an Angel and a Human a Nephil, but what of the other pairings?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T18:52:25-07:00","id":1131059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130065-thought-experiments?p=1130146#post1130146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would probably be super rare, but I don't see why not. Any Supernal entity with Life 4 could turn themselves into any animal they wanted, including human. A physical body would prevent Dissonance from destroying them and they could probably get around Mana bleed fairly easily if they were to latch on to a Mage.<br /> <br /> What would you call such children, and what powers (if any) would they have?<br /> <br /> I'd call the offspring of an Angel and a Human a Nephil, but what of the other pairings?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cambion for the S!demon hybrid, Alfar for SA!Fae, etc...honest'y I'd have multiple terms for each of them, as the phenomena is sufficiently rare that the terms are almost always reassigned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}